  "sourceCommit": "e2c3c817b2b482a535763695d19945971e19e41c",
  "sourceState": "Locally patched for native pointer-width safety, persistent circuit allocation and abc host integration. Hashes identify the distributed patched source, not unmodified upstream commit blobs. The cumulative full-world-pixels-v4-wld-host-hashing patch records WLD-only ABI 2, retained-pixel queries, default-OFF vanilla PixelBox rules, explicitly enabled restricted WireHead-style ordinary-pixel wave pairing with topology rejection, device dedup and semantics-preserving cold-load compile/read optimizations. OFF and ON have distinct pixel execution boundaries; shared physical gate-wave VM code is unchanged. Original/current hashes, removed-file identities, reference attribution and the reviewed diff are distributed under native/patches. The WLD Web export list additionally exposes the existing four incremental SHA-256 functions; the C hash implementation is unchanged.",
  "license": "No upstream license grant identified; inclusion is user-authorized and does not relicense upstream material.",
